	dc.b "on our planet we do not talk about such things in public",$00
    ; Appearance selects nine guarded replies, then one unconditional nine-choice record. Guards 1..9 match selected-choice +1..+9 writes; these are dialogue flags, not model IDs.
sConvPatternAppearance:
	dc.b "(what are I like/what are I/what do I look like)",$00
replyAppearance1Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $31	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm a big green lizard.",$00
replyAppearance2Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $32	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm a pink leopard.",$00
replyAppearance3Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $33	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm blue with 50 arms.",$00
replyAppearance4Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $34	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm small, green, and lobsterish.",$00
replyAppearance5Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $35	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm a massive bluebottle.",$00
replyAppearance6Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $36	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm a stripey 4d mouse.",$00
replyAppearance7Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $37	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm a 'human'.",$00
replyAppearance8Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $38	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I'm an obese green Pigoid (oink!).",$00
replyAppearance9Guard:
	dc.b $3F
	dc.b $39	; Leading ? opcode followed by conversation flag byte index; false skips to following NUL record
	dc.b "I told you, I am a pink mutant penguin with 7 wings, 3 beaks, 9 hands, and 14 different reproductive organs.",$00
    ; Exact ASCII/NUL appearance-choice record. Each selected alternative sets its own flag 1..9. Retain literal wording differences from guarded recalls; no physical alien identity is proved.
	dc.b "%r9(+1I am a lizardman./+2I am a pink leopard with shades on./+3I am a large blue pachyderm with 50 arms./+4I am a small green lobsterman./+5I am a massive bluebottleoid./+6I am a four dimensional rodent./+7I am a humanoid from a planet called Earth./+8I am a fat green Pigoid./+9I am a pink mutant penguin with 7 wings.)",$00
sConvPatternWantOrNeed:
	dc.b "you (want/need/desire) *=",$00
	dc.b "Why do you %1 %2?",$00
    ; This ship-description rule sets flag s ($73) in its outer reply. The audited table has no ?s guard; do not infer a ship-system write or close all possible flag readers.
sConvPatternShipDescription:
	dc.b "my ship (is/has) *",$00
	dc.b "+s%r3(Really, tell me about it/What's that like, I've never seen one/Tell me more)",$00
    ; This ship-needs reply also sets dialogue flag s before its literal question. Shared flag spelling does not establish object ownership, a model number or a gameplay transaction.
sConvPatternShipNeeds:
	dc.b "my ship needs *=",$00
